{
  "format": "supersilvia-workspace",
  "version": 1,
  "name": "A reading fed back",
  "kind": "video",
  "blurb": "A Tap reads the frame a dark disc is drawn into, and its reading sizes the disc",
  "layout": "linear",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "slug": "note",
      "pos": {
        "x": 40.0,
        "y": 40.0
      },
      "controls": {},
      "options": {},
      "values": {
        "text": {
          "Text": "A Tap's numbers are a frame old, so one may feed a node upstream of the Tap itself. Here its Mean, the frame's brightness, sizes the dark disc drawn into that frame: brighter noise grows the disc, which darkens the frame, which shrinks it again, so the disc breathes with the noise. The Slew eases each reading in; turn its Rise and Fall up and the disc answers faster."
        }
      },
      "width": 380.0
    },
